# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and put the real key there.
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` is gitignored. This file is not, and must never hold a real key.
# Restart the dev server after editing either -- Vite reads env at startup.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ===========================================================================
# READ THIS BEFORE PASTING A KEY
#
# Vite compiles every VITE_-prefixed variable INTO THE CLIENT BUNDLE. A key set
# below is downloaded by every visitor and readable in devtools in about ten
# seconds. That is a property of building a frontend with no server, not a
# mistake in this project.
#
# It is acceptable for local development and a laptop demo.
# It is NOT acceptable for anything you deploy to a public URL.
#
# So:
#   - use a key with a hard spend cap set in the OpenAI dashboard
#   - treat it as burnable, and revoke it after the round
#   - if you deploy, set VITE_EXPLAIN_PROXY instead and leave the key unset;
#     the key then lives on the proxy and never reaches the browser
# ===========================================================================

# Direct browser -> OpenAI. Local development only. Leave blank to keep the
# explanation docks running on the built-in offline matcher.
VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Defaults to gpt-4o-mini, which is cheap and widely available.
# Roughly a tenth of a US cent per question at this bundle size.
VITE_OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini

# Deployment path. If set, the app POSTs to this URL instead of OpenAI and
# sends NO key -- your proxy adds it server-side. Takes precedence over
# VITE_OPENAI_API_KEY when both are present.
#   e.g. VITE_EXPLAIN_PROXY=https://your-worker.example.dev/explain
VITE_EXPLAIN_PROXY=
